WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:21.649
"Way to go, Maggie!" Henry yelled. Cole let out a cheer too.

2
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:26.680
Maggie grinned proudly as Ms. Wood attached the blue ribbon to her pony's bridle.

3
00:00:26.681 --> 00:00:29.347
Most of the other riders looked happy too.

4
00:00:29.348 --> 00:00:37.397
Only one rider looked unhappy. That was Rebecca. She'd come in fourth.

5
00:00:37.398 --> 00:00:42.359
"I knew it!" she yelled, riding out of the ring and jumping down from her pony.

6
00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:45.280
"I would have won if I'd been riding Coco!"

7
00:00:45.281 --> 00:00:48.732
She flung her pony's reins away and kicked at the ground.

8
00:00:48.733 --> 00:00:53.106
Then she grabbed the white ribbon from the pony's bridle and stomped on it.

9
00:00:53.107 --> 00:00:57.841
"Rebecca!" Ms. Wood exclaimed. "You should be ashamed of yourself!

10
00:00:57.842 --> 00:01:00.200
That's very poor sportsmanship."

11
00:01:00.201 --> 00:01:02.487
"I don't care!" Rebecca yelled.

12
00:01:02.488 --> 00:01:08.634
"It's not fair! I wanted to ride Coco today. This stupid pony made me lose!"

13
00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:14.560
"Don't say that!" another girl spoke up. "Red is a great pony too."

14
00:01:14.561 --> 00:01:16.561
"Yeah," Maggie agreed.

15
00:01:16.562 --> 00:01:20.917
"I rode him once. He was awesome! Almost as good as Big Spot."

16
00:01:20.918 --> 00:01:24.353
"They're right, Rebecca." Ms. Wood sounded stern.

17
00:01:24.354 --> 00:01:27.337
"Now stop complaining and go take care of your pony.

18
00:01:27.338 --> 00:01:31.411
He did his best, and he deserves a nice grooming and some treats."

19
00:01:31.412 --> 00:01:33.878
A woman pushed through the crowd.

20
00:01:33.879 --> 00:01:37.777
"I think that's Rebecca's mother," Henry whispered to Cole.

21
00:01:37.778 --> 00:01:43.266
"Stop this tantrum right now and do as Ms. Wood says!" Rebecca's mother said.

22
00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:46.929
"Or you won't get to take riding lessons anymore."

23
00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:51.985
"Fine!" Rebecca cried. "But it's not fair!"

24
00:01:51.986 --> 00:01:56.232
She stomped off toward the barn, dragging her pony behind her.

25
00:01:56.233 --> 00:02:00.357
"Wow. Did you see that?" Henry said to Cole.

26
00:02:00.358 --> 00:02:05.257
"Rebecca is obviously still mad about not getting to ride Coco."

27
00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:10.918
Cole just shrugged. "Yeah. She's probably the shirt thief, like you said."

28
00:02:10.919 --> 00:02:16.610
Henry rubbed his chin thoughtfully. "She has a good motive.

29
00:02:16.611 --> 00:02:22.261
And she definitely could have done it. Now all we have to do is prove it."

30
00:02:22.262 --> 00:02:25.153
"That's not going to be easy," Cole said.

31
00:02:25.154 --> 00:02:29.486
"If there were any witnesses, somebody would have said something by now.

32
00:02:29.487 --> 00:02:35.738
Plus, if Rebecca hid that shirt somewhere, it will be tough to prove that she was the one who stole it.

33
00:02:35.739 --> 00:02:40.140
Maybe we should just forget about this case and focus on selling lemonade."

34
00:02:40.141 --> 00:02:44.993
Henry frowned at his friend. Cole wasn't acting like himself today.

35
00:02:44.994 --> 00:02:49.232
"The Lemonade Detectives agreed to accept this case.

36
00:02:49.233 --> 00:02:52.525
That means we need to try to solve it!

37
00:02:52.526 --> 00:02:56.942
If you don't want to help, Maggie and I can do it without you."

38
00:02:56.943 --> 00:03:02.031
Cole frowned too. "I'm not saying I don't want to help," he said.

39
00:03:02.032 --> 00:03:06.044
"I'm just saying it's not going to be easy to prove anything.

40
00:03:06.045 --> 00:03:11.158
Besides, Daisy's family lives in that big, fancy house over on Elm Street.

41
00:03:11.159 --> 00:03:16.759
They have plenty of money to buy her another shirt. So what's the big deal?"

42
00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:20.468
Henry was surprised to hear Cole say something like that.

43
00:03:20.469 --> 00:03:23.954
"Stealing is wrong!" he reminded Cole.

44
00:03:23.955 --> 00:03:29.600
"If Rebecca stole Daisy's shirt, she should give it back to Daisy and apologize.

45
00:03:29.601 --> 00:03:34.381
And if she didn't do it, we should figure out who did."

46
00:03:34.382 --> 00:03:37.847
Just then he saw Rebecca come stomping out of the barn.

47
00:03:37.848 --> 00:03:40.989
"There's our suspect now," Henry told Cole.

48
00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:45.075
"Stay with the lemonade stand. I'll be right back."

49
00:03:45.076 --> 00:03:48.120
Henry hurried off without waiting for an answer.

50
00:03:48.121 --> 00:03:50.970
He caught up to Rebecca near the parking lot.

51
00:03:50.971 --> 00:03:54.881
"Hi, Rebecca," he said. "Can I talk to you?"

52
00:03:54.882 --> 00:03:58.770
"Sure, what do you want to talk about?" Rebecca asked.

53
00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:03.895
Henry shrugged. "I just wanted to congratulate you," he said.

54
00:04:03.896 --> 00:04:06.940
"I saw you win fourth place just now.

55
00:04:06.941 --> 00:04:12.210
That's pretty good, especially since you didn't get to ride your favorite pony."

56
00:04:12.211 --> 00:04:15.001
"Tell me about it!" Rebecca scowled.

57
00:04:15.002 --> 00:04:20.172
"I still can't believe Daisy stole Coco from me! It's totally unfair!"

58
00:04:20.173 --> 00:04:23.941
"Yeah," Henry said, pretending to go along with her.

59
00:04:23.942 --> 00:04:28.024
"So did you go visit Coco in her stall earlier?

60
00:04:28.025 --> 00:04:30.738
You know, before the show started?"

61
00:04:30.739 --> 00:04:33.326
"Huh?" Rebecca blinked at him.

62
00:04:33.327 --> 00:04:38.356
"Yeah, I stopped by and gave her a carrot when I first got here. Why?"

63
00:04:38.357 --> 00:04:41.566
"Just curious." Henry cleared his throat.

64
00:04:41.567 --> 00:04:46.440
"Was that before or after Daisy arrived at the show?"

65
00:04:46.441 --> 00:04:48.991
"How should I know?" Rebecca said.

66
00:04:48.992 --> 00:04:52.399
"Why are you asking all these questions, anyway?"

67
00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:56.588
"I, uh . . ." Henry tried to think of something to say.

68
00:04:56.589 --> 00:05:00.404
Lots of people in Belltown knew about The Lemonade Detectives.

69
00:05:00.405 --> 00:05:05.488
If Rebecca had stolen that shirt, Henry didn't want her to guess that he knew she'd done it.

70
00:05:05.489 --> 00:05:08.334
Otherwise it might be even harder to prove.

71
00:05:08.335 --> 00:05:11.495
Just then Henry heard a clatter of hooves behind him.

72
00:05:11.496 --> 00:05:15.565
Turning, he saw Maggie rushing over, still leading Big Spot.

73
00:05:15.566 --> 00:05:20.683
"I need to talk to you, Henry," Maggie said breathlessly. "In private."

74
00:05:20.684 --> 00:05:26.970
She yanked him away from Rebecca.

75
00:05:26.971 --> 00:05:29.227
"What is it?" Henry asked.

76
00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:36.398
Maggie spun to face him. "I just found Daisy's missing shirt!"
